@0    = ~"The petite necromancer waded through the mud. He had but one goal: to bring back his dead kin, xvarts that had fallen during the infamous Battle on Graveyard. His plan was simple: to enchant the soil with the power of necromancy, and let undeath fill the rotting flesh of his dead brothers and sisters. But the necromancer didn't know there was a group of scouts patrolling the graveyard grounds."~
@1    = ~A xvart necromancer? Bah! Such a worthless creature should have never been allowed to use such power! (These pathetic things will never understand it's for potent minds—like that of Edwin Odesseiron.)~
@2    = ~If you want to face these enemies, face the necromancer, you should prepare yourself for dark magic. Oh, and you should also prepare 3,500 gold pieces.~
@3    = ~Right. Here's your gold.~
@4    = ~No. I'll pass. At least for now.~
@5    = ~Thank you. Try not to die, my friend.~
@6    = ~"The battle took a while, and while the xvart necromancer tried to use all the tricks he had, it wasn't enough. He fell in the very same spot where his kin had fallen a couple of tendays ago. When he was gone, and so were his undead allies, the place became quiet again."~
@7    = ~Who shall learn from this tale? Who shall learn how to protect themselves from the influence of even the darkest magic?~
@8    = ~<PLAYER1>.~
@9    = ~<PLAYER2>.~
@10   = ~<PLAYER3>.~
@11   = ~<PLAYER4>.~
@12   = ~<PLAYER5>.~
@13   = ~<PLAYER6>.~
@14   = ~They shall receive the gift.~
@15   = ~You've already faced the battle this book describes.~